{"sourceSha256": "64eb91d089befe59bd46fdca015f66b4fa13cfc840e611993dd7c6086b459f6a", "text": "Child Psychiatrist\nWickham Tce\nSpring Hill\nBrisbane\n\nDate: 03/07/2020\n\nDear Dr Bradshaw,\nRe: Jackson Martin\nDOB: 12/03/2011\n\n| am writing to refer Jackson, a 9-year-old primary school student. He has behavioural and\n\ndevelopmental features suggestive of a preliminary diagnosis of autistic spectrum cisorder.\n\nJackson lives with his mother, step-father and two step-brothers. His mother works in aged\ncare and has a significant history of drug abuse, binge drinking and depression.\n\nInitially, Jackson's parents brought him to the clinic at the age of 3 with concerns about his\nspeech. A developmental milestone assessment for speech and language was done and\n\nshowed delayed speech. Therefore, sessions with a speech therapist were arranged,\nalthough little improvement was noted at that time.\n\nOver the next 5 years, Jackson lived with his family in a rural area. In January 2020, his\nparents returned to Brisbane and presented today concermmed about Jackson's condition.\nThey reported a fist fight with other children, bouts of anger as well as decreasing school\nperformance over the past 2 school terms. Examination showed abnormal fascial expression,\nno eye contact and a minimal response to the questions. Jackson has difficulty making\nfriends and interacting with others. He prefers to play alone and displays a repetitive\nbehaviour of spinning and twirling around.\n\nIn view of the above, | believe Jackson requires a full psychiatric assessment. Please do not\n\nhesitate to contact me should you have any queries.", "pages": [{"number": 1, "text": "Child Psychiatrist\nWickham Tce\nSpring Hill\nBrisbane\n\nDate: 03/07/2020\n\nDear Dr Bradshaw,\nRe: Jackson Martin\nDOB: 12/03/2011\n\n| am writing to refer Jackson, a 9-year-old primary school student. He has behavioural and\n\ndevelopmental features suggestive of a preliminary diagnosis of autistic spectrum ciso